TEXT 664 136 Left 2 ;50 resonant frequencies
TEXT 16 112 Left 2 ;First Resonant frequency (6km)=3.163kHz accurate + 50 higher frequencis (only lower frequencies accurate)
TEXT 320 96 Left 2 !.param n=5
TEXT 392 -192 Left 2 ;The accuracy of the model depends of the element count (LC's) and the\nused frequencies in the circuit\nIf the circuit has low frequencies the concentrated model is accurate\nIf the frequencies are higher frequencies especially near resonant frequency\nthese models are becomming more and more  inaccurate.\nAt steady state there is only 50Hz(60Hz) and the concentrated model is accurate\n(see the accordance of all models at 50Hz)\nAt higher frequencies especially near resonant frequency more and more RC-ladders\nare neaded \nShort lines has higher resonant frequency therfore the concentrated model is longer valid\nLonger lines should have more and more LC's\nSinus shapes are also easier to transport as rectangele impulses since for rectangle \nimpulses there are many higher frequencies necessary (fourier)\n \nCables have lower resonant frequencies (approx. 4x) than overhead lines\nThe distributive lossless model at the toolbox is accurate and performs much faster in a\nsimulation. The ohmic part is modelled via a concentrated resistance
TEXT -24 248 Left 2 ;Left models are equivalent to right models\nbut left symbols are the original ltspice symbols
TEXT 488 248 Left 2 ;infinite higher\nresonant frequencies
TEXT -96 -72 Left 2 ;Resonant frequencies at concentrated model\nwith one or two LC-ladders are very inaccurate\ntherefore this model should only be used\n(especially if the linelength is long) if only\nlower frequencies are in the circuit
